    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0427" n="399" xml:id="pg399"/>

                <head>258. Memorandum From President Kennedy to Secretary of State Rusk<anchor n="0" xml:id="d258-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-07-05">July 5,
                    1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to your memorandum of July 1, 1961 concerning the latest
                    developments with regard to our Guinea Aid Program<anchor n="1" xml:id="d258-f2"
                    /> is there any chance that we could finance the big dam in Guinea if we omitted
                    all the other elements of our aid program? How much would we pay off dollar wise
                    to be able to do this?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
